Heaven Lost (World-Transformation): is the name of the current state of all of creation, the entire world governed by Mercurius's Hegemony Law, rather than merely the name of his personal combat technique. Its governing principle is his Hegemony Law, Acta Est Fabula, through which his Origin, Unknown emanates outwardly across creation and establishes an endless cycle of universal recurrence, and countless repeated alternative histories. Mercurius became the Throne God after reaching 「The Throne」, and his ascension fundamentally transformed all of existence. Under his dominion, every living being, including Divine Spirits, True Ancestors, Archetypes, Beasts, Machine Gods, Ultimate Ones, etc. possesses an individual identity and experiences its own unique life, but that life is destined to repeat again and again. When Mercurius encounters an ending that fails to satisfy his desire, his Law returns creation to an earlier state, restoring the world and its inhabitants so that the entire performance can begin anew. This is more than conventional time manipulation like Fifth Magic or the observation and traversal of parallel worlds like Second Magic: the recurrence is established as the fundamental governing principle of the world, operating across the infinite parallel universes and timelines encompassed by his dominion. Death, history, relationships, conflicts, and the development of civilizations become parts of an immense repeating performance, with countless lives unknowingly retracing paths they have already traveled. The recurrence preserves individual identity rather than simply replacing the dead with unrelated successors, making each person a recurring participant in the same cosmic drama. Certain individuals with particularly that have catch Mercurius interest are gifted to experience foreknowledge or déjà vu, faintly perceiving events from previous iterations and anticipating occurrences that should otherwise be unknown to them. Mercurius himself retains the full knowledge accumulated through these repetitions, leaving him burdened by an existence in which nearly every possibility has already been witnessed. Yet the world is not entirely without variation, since the existence of multiple possibilities and divergent developments is an important feature of the current world. His reign introduces the concept of endless possibility into the 「The Throne」's world, allowing the formation of a multiverse while keeping its countless histories from endless parallel worlds, timelines and possibilities subject to the overarching recurrence. The world of Heaven Lost is consequently an extension of his desire, not an independently operating mechanism that he merely controls from a distance. His greatest desire is to encounter something genuinely unknown and might ultimately die in the arms of Void Shiki, the woman whose existence offers the possibility of an ending beyond the repetition he has endured. Any conclusion other than the one he desires is unacceptable to him, and the world is therefore compelled to begin again whenever that dissatisfaction is expressed through his Law. This creates the central contradiction of Heaven Lost: its ruler has the power to renew existence on a cosmic scale, yet that same power prevents him from obtaining the genuine finality he seeks. The inhabitants of his world can live, struggle, love, and die without knowing how many times their stories have already unfolded, while Mercurius remains the spectator and playwright of an apparently interminable performance. Even his own death does not necessarily guarantee the conclusion of the recurrence, as the Law can enact a final renewal under the circumstances surrounding the succession of 「The Throne」. Heaven Lost is therefore both a metaphysical system of eternal repetition and the external manifestation of Mercurius's deepest psychological contradiction: a god who demands the unknown while continually restoring everything familiar, who possesses eternity but desires a particular death, and whose entire creation must continue repeating until the performance finally reaches the ending he will accept.

WEAKNESSES
Foreknowledge of Repetition: Mercurius also suffers from the consequences of his own Eternal Recurrence. His Law allows him to repeat existence whenever the conclusion is unacceptable, granting him opportunities to revise events and pursue different outcomes, but this same mechanism traps him within an existence dominated by repetition and foreknowledge. After witnessing countless cycles, he has become detached from ordinary experiences, finding little satisfaction in a reality whose developments are already familiar to him. His extraordinary knowledge does not provide genuine emotional fulfillment, and his longing for something unknown becomes increasingly difficult to satisfy within a world governed by his own predetermined repetitions. This is not a conventional weakness that reduces his destructive abilities, but it is a profound psychological limitation: the very power that allows him to reject undesirable conclusions perpetuates the circumstances from which he wishes to escape. His desire for an ideal future eventually diminishes until his longing to die in the unknown becomes his defining objective. 

Rejection of Endings: His refusal to accept any ending other than the one he desires is another fundamental limitation. Eternal Recurrence is the manifestation of this desire, meaning that the operation of his Law is intimately connected to his personal conception of an acceptable conclusion. Rather than being an entirely impartial ability that produces whatever outcome would be strategically optimal, it expresses Mercurius's determination to reject conclusions that fail to satisfy him. This makes his conduct comprehensible to someone who understands his underlying desire, even if predicting the precise details of his plans remains extraordinarily difficult. His immense power therefore does not free him from his own preferences; it enables him to enforce those preferences upon existence. In particular, knowledge of his desired ending has special relevance to confronting his ultimate destructive technique, Eager Denial of Truth, rather than merely functioning as an emotional observation. 

Diminished Manifestations: His manifested Sensories also possess a limitation that must be distinguished from the vulnerability of his true divine existence. Although they are extraordinarily powerful manifestations and are generally impervious to conventional physical phenomena, they are not identical in strength to Mercurius's true self. Consequently, overcoming or destroying a particular manifestation should not automatically be interpreted as permanently killing Mercurius himself. The distinction matters because his true existence operates at a level far beyond the ordinary physical world. Furthermore, Mercurius cannot utilize the Memory of the Throne and Akasha Records because of his paradoxical existence due to his law. It is a genuine restriction on the breadth of his available divine abilities, although it does not diminish the extraordinary capabilities of his own Law. Even though Mercurius states he has no interest on accessing Memory of the Throne and Akasha Records and his paradoxical existence makes Akasha Record’s information that is associated with “Mercurius” appear as paradoxically unfinished and recursively contradictory information that even Void Shiki can’t understand properly because it’s remains unfinished and keep looping back as a paradox back to when it was way more unfinished then it was and if he did try access Akasha Records and his existence was not paradoxical, he’ll likely be exposed to the same level of total knowledge as Void Shiki which he has no interest to since His Foreknowledge was already enough for him. Unfortunately for Renichi, information about him appears paradoxically unfinished as well due to connection with Mercurius.

Limits of God: Ultimately, Mercurius's greatest weakness is the contradiction between his virtually limitless capacity to control the circumstances of existence and his inability to manufacture the personal fulfillment he seeks through power alone. He can manipulate causality, repeat history, annihilate creation, and arrange events on a cosmic scale, yet none of these abilities inherently guarantees that Void Shiki will reciprocate his wishes, that he will experience genuine novelty, or that the conclusion of his existence will satisfy him since both of them share a lot in common with each other since the other understands what means to have too much knowledge. His formidable authority can be challenged by sufficiently powerful like Void Shiki, and his paradoxical nature restricts certain capabilities. Nevertheless, none of these weaknesses should be mistaken for a simple exploitable flaw that allows an ordinary opponent to defeat him. Mercurius is a god whose power allows him to reject almost every ending, but whose deepest desire makes him willing to accept one particular death.

How Throne God Truly "Die": Hadou Gods are fundamentally inapplicable to the conventional concept of death, just far more existential than lacking it. Because a Hadou God operates on the level of Taikyoku (their personal primal source of all dualities, concepts, and laws within their Origin), they transcend standard physical, spiritual, and conceptual vulnerabilities—including the concept of mortality itself. However, this can only be done by another God with equal or higher Taikyoku. When two Throne Gods clash, it is not a physical fight but a collision of their absolute respective laws. The entire universe under a specific Throne era is merely the outward expansion (Emanation) of that dominant Throne God's internal desire and Law. A "Concept of Death" only exists within a universe if a Throne God allows it or writes it into their specific Law because Death itself as whole concept is ultimately superseded like all concepts in the World due to a Throne God’s Taikyoku. Like how an Author cannot be killed by his own rules that written on script of paper they are holding instead being inside due to Throne God's power stems from Taikyoku (Taiji), which is their origin being emanated on all concepts in reality. Because they embody and command the very system that generates distinctions, including dualities (like life and death), they exist naturally outside of its boundaries. Meaning a Throne God with the weaker craving will have their Law painted over, crushed, and absorbed by the victor. In this sense, "death" for a Throne God means having their entire conceptual existence overwritten and consumed. Additionally, because Throne Gods are eternal and cannot die naturally by any other means in creation, which why their own souls possess a built-in self-destructive mechanism known as a True Death Cell. This is an internal "cancer cell" or manifestation born from a Throne God's own subconscious desire to self-destruct or end their eternal stagnation, which usually grows to match the Throne God’s Taikyoku and eventually kill them and True Death Cell will parish along their Originator as parish (e.g., Reinhardt acting as Mercurius's True Death Cell). In other words, True Death Cell like the Personal Embodiment of Death deeply connected to their respective Throne God that have kill when the Concept of Death itself couldn’t.
